Post Date: 2015-12-03T07:23:10Z
Current Date: April 4 2025
Title: Observable.combineLatest ignores onCompleted?
Description: Hello. This is the code:

``` java
import rx.Observable;
import rx.subjects.PublishSubject;

final class OnNextIngored {

   public static void main(final String[] args) {

      final PublishSubject<Integer> publisher = PublishSubject.create();

      // pass any arg to fail the day!
      final boolean doFail = args.length != 0;

      final Observable<Integer> possiblyFail
         = Observable.<Integer>create(subscriber
                                      -> {

                                         if (doFail) {
                                            subscriber.onError(new RuntimeException("blah"));
                                         } else {
                                            subscriber.onNext(2);
                                            subscriber.onCompleted();
                                         }
                                      });

      publisher
         .startWith(// combine latest ignores onCompleted ?
                    Observable.combineLatest(possiblyFail ,
                                             Observable.just(1),
                                             (l, r) -> r + l)
                    .take(2))
         .onErrorResumeNext(Observable.just(4))
         .subscribe(i -> {
               log("i is: " + i);
            },
            e -> {
               log("error is: " + e);
            },
            () -> {
               log("completed");
            } );

      publisher.onNext(5);
      publisher.onNext( 6 );
      publisher.onNext(7);
   }

   private static void log(final String s) {
      System.out.println(s);
   }
}
```

Depending on value of doFail (which can be changed by passing arg to test app) the conveyor receives or does not receive onCompleted and thus it does or does not ignore onNext:

```
[elk@qulix-elktop java-rxjava]$ java -cp rxjava-1.0.16.jar:. OnNextIngored 4
i is: 4
completed
[elk@qulix-elktop java-rxjava]$ java -cp rxjava-1.0.16.jar:. OnNextIngored 
i is: 3
i is: 5
i is: 6
i is: 7
```

Is it expected behavior? If yes, why?


